{
  "case_id": "2021-20-1088",
  "document_hash": "dfbb69b749e96a95db53be42b06f406dc63450fbd0dae4f9ede9c7f4c04b5512",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioners",
      "case_id": "2021-20-1088",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "dfbb69b749e96a95db53be42b06f406dc63450fbd0dae4f9ede9c7f4c04b5512",
      "evidence_id": "ev-dfbb69b749e9-0000-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. BINDAS: Mr. Chief Justice, and may it please the Court: Maine's sectarian exclusion discriminates based on religion. Like all discrimination based on religion, it should be subjected to strict scrutiny and held unconstitutional, unless Maine can show that it is necessary to achieve a compelling government interest."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Thomas",
      "case_id": "2021-20-1088",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "dfbb69b749e96a95db53be42b06f406dc63450fbd0dae4f9ede9c7f4c04b5512",
      "evidence_id": "ev-dfbb69b749e9-0000-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 6,
        "start": 6
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE THOMAS: Counsel, the -- neither of the two schools that you talk about, discuss, has indicated that it -- it will accept students who receive state funding or subsidies."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Barrett",
      "case_id": "2021-20-1088",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "dfbb69b749e96a95db53be42b06f406dc63450fbd0dae4f9ede9c7f4c04b5512",
      "evidence_id": "ev-dfbb69b749e9-0000-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 9,
        "start": 9
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE BARRETT: Well, would the Nelsons go to any place besides Temple Academy?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2021-20-1088",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "dfbb69b749e96a95db53be42b06f406dc63450fbd0dae4f9ede9c7f4c04b5512",
      "evidence_id": "ev-dfbb69b749e9-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 24,
        "start": 24
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAGAN: Can I take you back to Justice Breyer's point and also the Chief Justice's hypothetical, is you said, well, there's this, you know, strange use-status"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Bindas",
      "case_id": "2021-20-1088",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "dfbb69b749e96a95db53be42b06f406dc63450fbd0dae4f9ede9c7f4c04b5512",
      "evidence_id": "ev-dfbb69b749e9-0001-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 26,
        "start": 26
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. BINDAS: Your Honor, this is not subsidizing the -- the --the exercise of a right. It is conditioning the availability of an otherwise available public benefit on the surrender of a constitutional right. As this Court held in Thomas, the government cannot compel a citizen to choose between exercise of a right protected by the First Amendment and participation in an otherwise available public program."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Gorsuch",
      "case_id": "2021-20-1088",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "dfbb69b749e96a95db53be42b06f406dc63450fbd0dae4f9ede9c7f4c04b5512",
      "evidence_id": "ev-dfbb69b749e9-0001-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 28,
        "start": 28
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GORSUCH: Counsel, on that, I believe the government's response --and I think this is what Justice Kagan's getting at -- is in -- in -- in -- in Rust, you know, the question is whether you're put to a choice. And -- and, here, the government says there is no choice that you're put to because individuals can still educate their -- their children in religion by sending them to -- I think it's after-school programs or Saturday or Sunday programs."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Bindas",
      "case_id": "2021-20-1088",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "dfbb69b749e96a95db53be42b06f406dc63450fbd0dae4f9ede9c7f4c04b5512",
      "evidence_id": "ev-dfbb69b749e9-0001-0004",
      "kind": "allegation",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 36,
        "start": 36
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I mean, these schools are overtly discriminatory. They're proudly discriminatory."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "MR. BINDAS",
      "case_id": "2021-20-1088",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "dfbb69b749e96a95db53be42b06f406dc63450fbd0dae4f9ede9c7f4c04b5512",
      "evidence_id": "ev-dfbb69b749e9-0002-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 45,
        "start": 45
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "That is correct, Your Honor. We -- we are not arguing that there is a constitutional right to a publicly funded religious education, nor could we. Espinoza said point blank a state need not subsidize private education."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "JUSTICE THOMAS",
      "case_id": "2021-20-1088",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "dfbb69b749e96a95db53be42b06f406dc63450fbd0dae4f9ede9c7f4c04b5512",
      "evidence_id": "ev-dfbb69b749e9-0002-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 50,
        "start": 50
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Counsel, in Maine, can a parent decide that they simply do not want to send their child to any school at all?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "JUSTICE ALITO",
      "case_id": "2021-20-1088",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "dfbb69b749e96a95db53be42b06f406dc63450fbd0dae4f9ede9c7f4c04b5512",
      "evidence_id": "ev-dfbb69b749e9-0002-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 55,
        "start": 55
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Suppose parents want to send their child, using this money, to an elite private school, Exeter, Andover, Miss Porter's. That would be okay, right?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2021-20-1088",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "dfbb69b749e96a95db53be42b06f406dc63450fbd0dae4f9ede9c7f4c04b5512",
      "evidence_id": "ev-dfbb69b749e9-0003-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 66,
        "start": 66
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Well, then you really are discriminating on the basis of religious belief. What I described is, I think, pretty close to Unitarian Universalism, isn't it? And that is a -- that is a religious community."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Barrett",
      "case_id": "2021-20-1088",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "dfbb69b749e96a95db53be42b06f406dc63450fbd0dae4f9ede9c7f4c04b5512",
      "evidence_id": "ev-dfbb69b749e9-0004-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 88,
        "start": 88
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE BARRETT: But the statute says non-sectarian. It doesn't say religiously neutral, right?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Maine Department of Education",
      "case_id": "2021-20-1088",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "dfbb69b749e96a95db53be42b06f406dc63450fbd0dae4f9ede9c7f4c04b5512",
      "evidence_id": "ev-dfbb69b749e9-0004-0004",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 88,
        "start": 88
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. TAUB: Well, that's true. But -- but I think that -- that -- that the spirit and purpose of the program -- and -- and -- and we've talked about this with the commissioner of the Department of Education, and -- and -- and her position is -- is the same as ours, that -- that a school that is --that is antireligious is not religiously neutral, and so it would not qualify for this program."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Malcolm L. Stewart",
      "case_id": "2021-20-1088",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "dfbb69b749e96a95db53be42b06f406dc63450fbd0dae4f9ede9c7f4c04b5512",
      "evidence_id": "ev-dfbb69b749e9-0004-0003",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 93,
        "start": 93
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. STEWART: Thank you, Mr. Chief Justice, and may it please the Court: The judgment of the court of appeals upholding Maine's sectarian school exclusion should be affirmed. That is so for three basic reasons."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Thomas",
      "case_id": "2021-20-1088",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "dfbb69b749e96a95db53be42b06f406dc63450fbd0dae4f9ede9c7f4c04b5512",
      "evidence_id": "ev-dfbb69b749e9-0004-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 94,
        "start": 94
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE THOMAS: Mr. Stewart, what exactly is an anti-establishment interest and where does it come from?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Gorsuch",
      "case_id": "2021-20-1088",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "dfbb69b749e96a95db53be42b06f406dc63450fbd0dae4f9ede9c7f4c04b5512",
      "evidence_id": "ev-dfbb69b749e9-0004-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 107,
        "start": 107
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GORSUCH: Mr. Stewart, I do -- I do have one question. I -- I -- I just want to confirm my understanding. I -- I didn't see in the government's brief any strict reliance or suggestion that the Court should rely on a status-use distinction. Rather, I saw this analogy to government speech. Is that right?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Stewart",
      "case_id": "2021-20-1088",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "dfbb69b749e96a95db53be42b06f406dc63450fbd0dae4f9ede9c7f4c04b5512",
      "evidence_id": "ev-dfbb69b749e9-0005-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 108,
        "start": 108
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. STEWART: No, but we don't view the status-use distinction as being based, as -- as Justice Kagan was saying earlier, on a distinction between religious belief and religious conduct. We -- we think the status-use distinction means, on the one hand, the state can decline to fund your religious exercise, but it cannot define -- decline to give you an unrelated benefit based on the fact that you have engaged in religious exercise outside the program."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Gorsuch",
      "case_id": "2021-20-1088",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "dfbb69b749e96a95db53be42b06f406dc63450fbd0dae4f9ede9c7f4c04b5512",
      "evidence_id": "ev-dfbb69b749e9-0005-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 119,
        "start": 119
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GORSUCH: Including on the basis of sex and race and other personal characteristics like that?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Bindas",
      "case_id": "2021-20-1088",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "dfbb69b749e96a95db53be42b06f406dc63450fbd0dae4f9ede9c7f4c04b5512",
      "evidence_id": "ev-dfbb69b749e9-0005-0002",
      "kind": "allegation",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 122,
        "start": 122
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. BINDAS: Starting with the United States' arguments, this absolutely discriminates against parents. It says you can get an otherwise available public benefit you are statutorily entitled to so long as you don't exercise a right that this Court recognized in Espinoza."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Source extraction",
      "case_id": "2021-20-1088",
      "confidence": 0.0,
      "document_hash": "dfbb69b749e96a95db53be42b06f406dc63450fbd0dae4f9ede9c7f4c04b5512",
